            <div xml:id="d129">

                <pb facs="0324" n="292" xml:id="pg292"/>

                <head>129. Memorandum From the Assistant Secretary of State for Far Eastern Affairs
                        (Bundy) to President
                        Johnson<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d129-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1965-02-16">February 16,
                        1965</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Per your request this afternoon,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d129-f2"/> Ambassador
                        Thompson and I have done the attached
                    summary of reactions by key countries to our actions in Viet-Nam.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d129-f3"/></p>
                <p>To summarize briefly, the score card reads: <list>
                        <item><hi rendition="#italic">With us pretty strongly</hi>
                            <list>
                                <item>Thailand</item>
                                <item>Philippines</item>
                                <item>Australia</item>
                                <item>New Zealand</item>
                                <item>Taiwan</item>
                                <item>South Korea</item>
                                <item>Laos</item>
                                <item>Germany</item>
                            </list></item>
                        <item><hi rendition="#italic">With us, but wobbly on negotiations</hi>
                            <list>
                                <item>UK</item>
                                <item>Canada</item>
                                <item>India</item>
                            </list></item>
                        <item><hi rendition="#italic">With us tepidly</hi>
                            <list>
                                <item>Japan</item>
                                <item>Malaysia</item>
                                <item>Italy and other NATO
                                    allies</item>
                                <item>Latin America</item>
                            </list></item>
                        <item><hi rendition="#italic">Skeptical or opposed</hi>
                            <list>
                                <item>France</item>
                                <item>Pakistan</item>
                            </list></item>
                        <item><hi rendition="#italic">Mixed</hi>
                            <list>
                                <item>Africa</item>
                            </list></item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>We have left out the neutralist Afro-Asian countries, such as Indonesia, most of
                    which are opposed—some vehemently, but some also with an underlying appreciation
                    of what we are doing.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">William P.
                                Bundy</hi><anchor n="4" xml:id="d129-f4"
                    /></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
